---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
warning[manual_index_counter]: `n` always equals `it_index` of the loop that follows
  --> tests/lint/manual_index_counter/bad.jai:4:5
   |
 4 |     n := 0;
   |     ^
   |
help: use `it_index` instead of counting by hand
   |
 4 -     n := 0;
 7 -         print("% %\n", n, it);
 8 -         n += 1;
 6 +         print("% %\n", it_index, it);
   |
   = note: `manual_index_counter` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/manual_index_counter

warning[manual_index_counter]: `line_number` always equals `it_index` of the loop that follows
  --> tests/lint/manual_index_counter/bad.jai:13:5
   |
13 |     line_number := 0;
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: use `it_index` instead of counting by hand
   |
13 -     line_number := 0;
16 -         defer line_number += 1;
16 ~         print("%: %\n", it_index, it);
   |
   = note: `manual_index_counter` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/manual_index_counter

